course: dictionary
lesson: 15820
title: Uncontrolled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uncontrolled means not controlled or held back. Something uncontrolled runs wild, with nothing holding it in. «The uncontrolled fire spread across the dry field in minutes.» The fire was not held back, so it was wild and dangerous.
explain: The word is made from un- (not) and controlled (held back or managed). Take away un- and you get controlled, which is the opposite. «Uncontrolled laughter» means laughing that cannot be held in, not laughing that is kept neat and quiet.
explain: Uncontrolled can also mean not checked or managed by rules or people. «The uncontrolled building of houses worried the village.» Nobody was checking where or how the houses were built. Try your meaning in the sentence: "not held back" or "not checked" should both make sense.
fact: Uncontrolled means not controlled or held back, often in a wild or dangerous way.
fact: «Uncontrolled bleeding» means blood flowing with no way of being stopped, so help is needed quickly.
fact: In a science test, an uncontrolled variable is something you forgot to keep the same, which makes the test unfair.
fact: «Uncontrolled anger» shows strong feelings that burst out without being held back.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so uncontrolled is the opposite of controlled.
exercise: «The uncontrolled fire spread across the dry field.» What does uncontrolled mean here? | Calm and safe | Very small | *Wild and not held back | Put out quickly
exercise: In a science test, what is an uncontrolled variable? | *Something you forgot to keep the same, which makes the test unfair | The equipment you used to measure | The result you measured at the end | A rule that the teacher wrote
exercise: «The uncontrolled dog ran into the road.» Find and copy one word that means the dog was not held back. | dog | road | ran | *uncontrolled
test: «Uncontrolled bleeding needs help quickly.» What does uncontrolled mean here? | Very slow and gentle | *Not held back, flowing with no way of stopping | Stopped for good | Painful but harmless
test: «The uncontrolled building of houses worried the village.» What does uncontrolled suggest? | Built by children | *Built with no rules or checks | Built on the sea | Built with careful plans and rules
exam: Which meaning fits «uncontrolled anger»? | Anger that is short and polite | *Anger that bursts out and is not held back | A kind of happy feeling | Anger that is carefully managed and kept quiet
